WEBVTT

00:00:19.490 --> 00:00:26.750
<i>New days, it's the morning we begin. 
Let's give the world a kiss.</i>

00:00:27.710 --> 00:00:35.240
<i>Blowing in the wind, with a little 
courage and love in our pockets.</i>

00:00:37.140 --> 00:00:44.090
<i>I wish: If only I had wings,</i>

00:00:45.390 --> 00:00:53.690
<i>I could fly over the sadness, 
the past, and my doubts.</i>

00:00:53.690 --> 00:01:02.450
<i>Oh, yeah! There's nothing to lose. 
(Take whatever the brand new day brings.)</i>

00:01:02.450 --> 00:01:07.290
<i>Take my way! I wanna catch a miracle...</i>

00:01:07.290 --> 00:01:11.030
<i>in the palm of my hand!</i>

00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:19.720
<i>We're off on a journey through the endless 
earth, the skies, and the future.</i>

00:01:20.290 --> 00:01:32.140
<i>I know these newborn wings, oh! 
Are gonna gonna gonna shine someday!</i>

00:01:36.450 --> 00:01:38.910
Let us out! Let us out of here!

00:01:38.910 --> 00:01:40.240
This guy is getting on my nerves...

00:01:40.240 --> 00:01:41.450
Shut up back there!

00:01:42.160 --> 00:01:43.680
Do what you will with me,

00:01:43.680 --> 00:01:45.870
but let Miss Pacifica go!

00:01:45.870 --> 00:01:47.750
If you don't stop making all that racket,

00:01:48.050 --> 00:01:49.250
I'm going to kill you.

00:02:00.020 --> 00:02:01.180
Um...

00:02:01.780 --> 00:02:05.390
What's going to happen to me?

00:02:07.180 --> 00:02:09.060
I don't really know who she is.

00:02:09.060 --> 00:02:12.360
Did this Scrapped Princess person 
really do such bad things?

00:02:21.280 --> 00:02:26.290
"Aria of a Mother's Sorrow"

00:02:28.210 --> 00:02:28.750
Get in!

00:02:29.420 --> 00:02:30.710
Huh? H-Hey!

00:02:32.920 --> 00:02:34.440
Ow...

00:02:35.130 --> 00:02:36.770
What did you do <i>that </i>for?!

00:02:38.970 --> 00:02:40.430
What's that for?

00:02:40.430 --> 00:02:43.510
Do they expect me to do my business in <i>that</i>?

00:02:44.100 --> 00:02:45.740
That's so mean!

00:02:45.740 --> 00:02:47.730
It's like this is a dungeon or something!

00:02:47.730 --> 00:02:49.860
Oh. I guess it <i>is </i>a dungeon.

00:02:51.230 --> 00:02:53.480
I can't even take a bath in here...

00:02:55.360 --> 00:02:56.820
Leo...

00:02:56.820 --> 00:02:58.100
Winia...

00:02:59.950 --> 00:03:01.270
Furet...

00:03:13.010 --> 00:03:13.920
Come here.

00:03:38.110 --> 00:03:39.830
Um... Hello?

00:03:39.830 --> 00:03:41.450
Are you all right in there?

00:03:41.450 --> 00:03:43.320
Y-Yes...

00:03:44.170 --> 00:03:45.280
Thank you.

00:03:47.700 --> 00:03:49.330
You've captured the Scrapped Princess?

00:03:49.330 --> 00:03:50.330
Yes, sir.

00:03:50.330 --> 00:03:51.000
I see.

00:03:51.790 --> 00:03:55.750
However, she has yet to admit to that.

00:03:55.750 --> 00:03:56.500
That's all right.

00:03:56.850 --> 00:03:57.880
But, sir...

00:03:57.880 --> 00:03:59.960
An imposter will do just as well.

00:04:00.530 --> 00:04:02.290
The fact that we captured her...

00:04:02.290 --> 00:04:04.470
That is what is important.

00:04:05.300 --> 00:04:07.430
They've captured the Scrapped Princess,

00:04:07.430 --> 00:04:09.600
and we're still going 
to stand back and watch?

00:04:09.600 --> 00:04:13.520
It will be another 200 hours before 
the princess turns sixteen.

00:04:13.520 --> 00:04:15.600
Let's see how things develop a while longer.

00:04:15.600 --> 00:04:19.440
These foolish creatures will probably 
put on an amusing show for us.

00:04:19.440 --> 00:04:22.700
Toying with the humans is a waste of time.

00:04:22.700 --> 00:04:25.660
For us, it is a meaningless act.

00:04:25.660 --> 00:04:27.450
You find it disagreeable?

00:04:27.450 --> 00:04:33.250
Even so, our personalities were modeled 
after those cruel, foul-tempered humans.

00:04:33.250 --> 00:04:34.670
Don't forget that.

00:04:39.630 --> 00:04:41.880
You can go now.

00:04:42.260 --> 00:04:44.840
We don't need you anymore. Go away.

00:04:45.970 --> 00:04:47.300
What have you done with Miss Pacifica?

00:04:47.300 --> 00:04:49.670
Just go away!

00:04:49.670 --> 00:04:51.140
Wait! Hey, wait!

00:04:52.020 --> 00:04:54.350
Open up! Open this door!

00:04:54.350 --> 00:04:55.600
Open this door!

00:04:57.770 --> 00:04:59.060
Please, I beg you...

00:05:00.390 --> 00:05:01.750
Open the door.

00:05:04.450 --> 00:05:05.920
Open the door.

00:05:06.740 --> 00:05:07.700
Leo...

00:05:08.450 --> 00:05:10.040
I promised him.

00:05:10.760 --> 00:05:11.740
I gave him my word...

00:05:12.910 --> 00:05:15.880
I said I would keep Miss 
Pacifica safe, no matter what.

00:05:16.920 --> 00:05:19.210
I gave him my word...

00:05:25.590 --> 00:05:27.280
Is this the right thing to do?

00:05:28.040 --> 00:05:29.860
This way, we won't be disbanded.

00:05:29.860 --> 00:05:30.680
That's all that matters, right?

00:05:31.100 --> 00:05:33.460
Chris... Jill...

00:05:33.460 --> 00:05:37.100
Word's come down that Prince Forsyth is 
going to be sent away to the holy city.

00:05:37.550 --> 00:05:38.480
What?!

00:05:38.480 --> 00:05:41.360
He apparently scolded the king,

00:05:41.360 --> 00:05:43.070
telling him to treat the 
Scrapped Princess better.

00:05:44.030 --> 00:05:47.570
It sounds like the prince has been advising 
him against going to war this whole time.

00:05:48.110 --> 00:05:51.500
I guess the king wants to get 
rid of his troublemaker son.

00:05:52.030 --> 00:05:53.770
Say, Chris...

00:05:53.770 --> 00:05:56.720
Even if it means losing the unit,

00:05:56.720 --> 00:05:58.540
you know we'll follow you.

00:05:59.120 --> 00:06:02.000
What is it that you really want to do?

00:06:08.450 --> 00:06:11.220
Hey, did you guys get that notice, too?

00:06:11.220 --> 00:06:12.430
Yeah, we did!

00:06:13.390 --> 00:06:16.560
I guess this means that they 
caught the Scrapped Princess.

00:06:16.560 --> 00:06:18.890
Yeah. Looks like we'll 
have it easy for a while.

00:06:19.310 --> 00:06:20.600
Is that true?

00:06:21.560 --> 00:06:22.840
Must be.

00:06:22.840 --> 00:06:25.860
They rescinded our orders to search for her.

00:06:26.320 --> 00:06:28.030
Where are they keeping her?

00:06:28.030 --> 00:06:30.360
She's probably already been executed by now.

00:06:30.360 --> 00:06:33.620
After all, she's the poison 
that'll destroy the world.

00:06:33.620 --> 00:06:36.580
They said she had an ugly, evil-lookin' face.

00:06:40.620 --> 00:06:42.960
Ow!

00:06:42.960 --> 00:06:43.960
Hey, you bastard!

00:06:48.380 --> 00:06:51.390
Watch where you're putting that right hand!

00:06:51.390 --> 00:06:53.050
Are you ready to face the consequences?

00:06:53.800 --> 00:06:56.060
This doesn't bode well.

00:06:56.060 --> 00:06:59.440
You're so irritated that you have 
stopped thinking your actions through.

00:06:59.440 --> 00:07:01.730
You're part of the reason 
that I'm so irritated!

00:07:01.730 --> 00:07:02.810
What are you people doing?

00:07:03.900 --> 00:07:05.270
Stand aside!

00:07:09.570 --> 00:07:11.410
Shannon Cassul, I presume?

00:07:11.410 --> 00:07:12.450
And you are?

00:07:13.280 --> 00:07:17.330
We're the Royal Forces Intelligence Bureau, 
Special Operations Disposal Squad.

00:07:17.330 --> 00:07:18.700
The Blackhawks, huh?

00:07:19.410 --> 00:07:22.000
I'm the squad leader, Luke Sturm.

00:07:22.000 --> 00:07:23.500
What do you want with me?

00:07:23.500 --> 00:07:24.670
I'd like you to come with us.

00:07:25.790 --> 00:07:29.840
We would also like the woman with you, 
the Peacemaker, to accompany us as well.

00:07:31.630 --> 00:07:33.980
Let me make this clear.

00:07:33.980 --> 00:07:37.220
At this point in time, we have 
no intention of antagonizing

00:07:37.220 --> 00:07:39.640
either you or the forces of the Peacemakers.

00:07:40.430 --> 00:07:43.600
I'd like you to think of this 
as nothing more than a request.

00:07:44.770 --> 00:07:47.060
This "request" of yours 
comes at a bad time...

00:07:47.900 --> 00:07:49.570
All right. Let's go.

00:07:59.700 --> 00:08:01.000
They have Pacifica?!

00:08:01.000 --> 00:08:02.160
I'm sorry...

00:08:02.660 --> 00:08:06.130
I knew it would be difficult for her 
to escape, but I didn't expect her

00:08:06.130 --> 00:08:08.000
to be caught so soon...

00:08:08.000 --> 00:08:10.510
And I still don't know where Shannon is...

00:08:10.510 --> 00:08:12.170
I'll do all I can to rescue her!

00:08:12.460 --> 00:08:13.630
And how will you do that?

00:08:13.980 --> 00:08:16.300
Arrange a jailbreak, or 
set off a mass escape...

00:08:16.300 --> 00:08:17.470
There are all sorts of ways.

00:08:17.470 --> 00:08:19.430
That doesn't sound very practical...

00:08:19.430 --> 00:08:21.100
Then we'll use Miss Raquel's magic!

00:08:21.730 --> 00:08:23.680
We can't make any rash moves,

00:08:23.680 --> 00:08:25.690
not without knowing what sort 
of shape Pacifica is in.

00:08:25.690 --> 00:08:28.860
What about that Inquisitor friend of yours?

00:08:28.860 --> 00:08:32.130
He's been summoned to the castle...

00:08:32.130 --> 00:08:33.860
If I could meet with Berkens,

00:08:33.860 --> 00:08:37.320
maybe I could learn something 
about Pacifica...

00:08:40.580 --> 00:08:43.080
Highness. By order of His Majesty,

00:08:43.570 --> 00:08:46.580
I am to take you to the holy city.

00:08:47.060 --> 00:08:48.380
Father's orders?

00:08:48.380 --> 00:08:50.920
The capital is in turmoil,

00:08:50.920 --> 00:08:54.680
so he believes this to be in 
Your Highness' best interest.

00:08:56.230 --> 00:08:58.530
I've heard that the Scrapped 
Princess has been captured.

00:08:59.100 --> 00:09:02.560
Would it be possible for me to at 
least see my sister before I leave?

00:09:03.100 --> 00:09:04.520
As to that...

00:09:06.600 --> 00:09:07.980
I suppose it's too much to ask.

00:09:12.440 --> 00:09:14.630
Hey, are you really okay over there?

00:09:14.630 --> 00:09:16.360
You don't sound very good.

00:09:16.360 --> 00:09:19.410
Yes... What about you? Are you all right?

00:09:19.700 --> 00:09:21.990
Yes, thanks, miss.

00:09:23.120 --> 00:09:26.790
I may not look it, but I 
have a daughter and a son...

00:09:26.790 --> 00:09:28.850
How old are you?

00:09:28.850 --> 00:09:30.250
I'm not really sure.

00:09:30.250 --> 00:09:31.250
Huh?

00:09:31.250 --> 00:09:33.630
Well, I sorta lost my memory.

00:09:33.630 --> 00:09:35.880
Oh, I see... You poor dear.

00:09:36.380 --> 00:09:38.970
That's why I don't really 
understand what's going on.

00:09:39.640 --> 00:09:41.850
Why did they take me prisoner?

00:09:41.850 --> 00:09:44.700
Out of the blue, they say I'm the 
Scrapped Princess or whatever.

00:09:44.700 --> 00:09:46.140
I don't get it.

00:09:46.140 --> 00:09:49.310
Scrapped Princess?

00:09:50.560 --> 00:09:52.820
Ma'am? Are you okay?

00:09:53.730 --> 00:09:55.430
Y-Yes...

00:09:56.030 --> 00:09:57.780
Ma'am, why did they throw you in here?

00:10:00.200 --> 00:10:04.240
I secretly let a person get away 
that everyone wanted to kill...

00:10:04.750 --> 00:10:07.580
They tortured me, wanting to 
know where this person is...

00:10:07.580 --> 00:10:10.180
But that person's been captured now,

00:10:10.180 --> 00:10:11.920
so I suppose they no longer need me...

00:10:12.840 --> 00:10:15.300
This person must have meant a lot to you...

00:10:15.300 --> 00:10:16.170
Yes...

00:10:16.900 --> 00:10:19.720
But he got captured... Poor guy...

00:10:36.400 --> 00:10:39.110
Your hand is cold.

00:10:40.320 --> 00:10:43.080
No, your hands are warm...

00:10:45.660 --> 00:10:48.250
I have a message from General Peters-Stahl.

00:10:48.250 --> 00:10:52.580
It reads, "I consider it an honor that 
you have agreed to meet with me."

00:10:52.580 --> 00:10:55.500
I don't have time to engage in 
pointless social pleasantries.

00:10:55.500 --> 00:10:56.550
Get to the point.

00:10:58.130 --> 00:11:00.630
It's to be expected from a Peacemaker.

00:11:00.630 --> 00:11:02.640
You may have taken on human form,

00:11:02.640 --> 00:11:05.970
but it looks like human common sense and 
manners are foreign concepts to you.

00:11:05.970 --> 00:11:08.310
You people are the ones with no manners here.

00:11:08.310 --> 00:11:11.520
Did you only ask us here because you 
wanted to make sarcastic remarks at us?

00:11:12.020 --> 00:11:14.440
Calm yourself, Shannon Cassul.

00:11:14.440 --> 00:11:16.480
Come with me, please.

00:11:22.840 --> 00:11:23.750
Enter.

00:11:27.330 --> 00:11:29.620
General. I have brought him.

00:11:31.080 --> 00:11:32.580
I'll get right to the point.

00:11:34.080 --> 00:11:36.550
We want to join forces with you.

00:11:44.800 --> 00:11:46.230
What do you mean by that?

00:11:46.770 --> 00:11:49.220
Our research shows that the 
beings known as the Peacemakers

00:11:49.220 --> 00:11:53.310
have meddled in our world from the shadows,

00:11:53.310 --> 00:11:54.480
and have manipulated our history.

00:11:55.270 --> 00:11:56.820
And?

00:11:56.820 --> 00:12:00.240
Nevertheless, we intend to march on Giat

00:12:00.240 --> 00:12:03.160
with or without the permission 
of the Peacemakers.

00:12:03.160 --> 00:12:06.450
And, in turn, become masters of the world.

00:12:07.530 --> 00:12:09.080
The reasons why are unclear,

00:12:09.080 --> 00:12:12.460
but the Scrapped Princess seems to be 
the only threat to the Peacemakers.

00:12:13.120 --> 00:12:16.380
And that Scrapped Princess is in 
our custody at this very moment.

00:12:21.340 --> 00:12:23.800
You're planning to use my 
sister as a bargaining chip?

00:12:24.300 --> 00:12:25.700
Give her to me!

00:12:26.800 --> 00:12:27.760
Calm yourself.

00:12:27.760 --> 00:12:29.810
Where's Pacifica?!

00:12:29.810 --> 00:12:31.560
The Scrapped Princess is unharmed.

00:12:31.560 --> 00:12:35.060
Incidentally, I am told that 
you have combat capabilities

00:12:35.060 --> 00:12:37.480
that are on par with 
those of the Peacemakers.

00:12:37.940 --> 00:12:42.570
With your assistance, we could 
easily conquer the world.

00:12:42.570 --> 00:12:43.450
Are you serious?

00:12:44.150 --> 00:12:45.310
Are you crazy?

00:12:45.310 --> 00:12:47.910
Do you seriously think you can 
negotiate with the Peacemakers?

00:12:47.910 --> 00:12:50.740
You're going to demand that 
they let you rule the world?

00:12:50.740 --> 00:12:53.410
Because I believe it to 
be the right thing to do.

00:12:53.410 --> 00:12:56.370
You think it's right? Right for who?

00:12:58.500 --> 00:13:00.340
I see you don't intend to assist us.

00:13:00.340 --> 00:13:02.460
Assist you, huh?

00:13:02.460 --> 00:13:04.220
I suggest that you don't forget one thing.

00:13:04.220 --> 00:13:08.850
Your precious sister is in our hands.

00:13:09.600 --> 00:13:11.310
I'll ask you again later.

00:13:11.310 --> 00:13:14.270
In the meantime, I suggest that you 
give the matter a good deal of thought.

00:13:15.730 --> 00:13:16.810
This way.

00:13:16.810 --> 00:13:17.770
I know.

00:13:20.520 --> 00:13:22.190
You, huh?

00:13:22.190 --> 00:13:23.740
A Peacemaker?

00:13:23.740 --> 00:13:24.920
No.

00:13:25.490 --> 00:13:27.200
Oh, one of those Dragoons.

00:13:27.700 --> 00:13:29.270
Give us a minute.

00:13:29.270 --> 00:13:31.200
I'm not dumb enough to try to escape.

00:13:32.870 --> 00:13:35.480
I'll be waiting for you 
in the antechamber, then.

00:13:38.380 --> 00:13:39.360
Shannon,

00:13:40.470 --> 00:13:43.590
Pacifica appears to be 
in this castle's dungeon.

00:13:44.880 --> 00:13:47.550
It must be difficult for 
you to feel so helpless.

00:13:48.720 --> 00:13:52.500
I never expected you to take my 
feelings into account about anything.

00:13:53.140 --> 00:13:56.430
I wish... I wish to help you.

00:13:56.430 --> 00:14:00.150
Oh, that's right. I remember something 
about me being your master.

00:14:00.150 --> 00:14:01.370
That is true.

00:14:01.370 --> 00:14:04.570
But I wish to help you of my own free will.

00:14:05.710 --> 00:14:07.310
Do not forget.

00:14:07.310 --> 00:14:09.950
Should you ever need me, call my name.

00:14:09.950 --> 00:14:12.780
I will be at your side.

00:14:28.090 --> 00:14:29.800
Eirote!

00:14:29.800 --> 00:14:30.820
Ma'am?

00:14:30.820 --> 00:14:33.140
How much longer before we can activate them?

00:14:33.140 --> 00:14:35.350
It will be another 30 hours or so.

00:14:35.930 --> 00:14:38.180
It's impressive that you 
were able to complete them

00:14:38.180 --> 00:14:40.440
in such a short amount of time.

00:14:40.440 --> 00:14:43.570
They were designed by humans 
no different from us.

00:14:43.570 --> 00:14:45.360
You shouldn't underestimate us.

00:14:45.360 --> 00:14:48.320
I just received a message from Zefiris.

00:14:49.070 --> 00:14:52.530
She says that Pacifica Cassul has 
been captured by the kingdom.

00:14:52.530 --> 00:14:53.650
She's what?

00:14:55.790 --> 00:14:57.000
Eirote!

00:14:57.000 --> 00:14:57.910
Ma'am?

00:14:57.910 --> 00:15:00.460
I want these Gigases 
activated in three hours.

00:15:01.780 --> 00:15:02.460
Yes, ma'am!

00:15:12.140 --> 00:15:13.550
It's no use.

00:15:13.550 --> 00:15:15.850
No matter how often I try, 
I can't locate Shannon.

00:15:16.350 --> 00:15:18.600
Something is jamming me.

00:15:18.600 --> 00:15:21.730
It's possible that there might 
be a Peacemaker near him.

00:15:21.730 --> 00:15:24.730
I suppose all we can do 
now is sit back and pray.

00:15:26.900 --> 00:15:31.220
No. Begging the gods for help 
is nothing but a waste of time.

00:15:34.700 --> 00:15:36.610
There's no point in staying here.

00:15:37.330 --> 00:15:38.750
I have to do something, 
even if it's on my own.

00:15:43.290 --> 00:15:46.670
I hope Pacifica is all right.

00:15:47.130 --> 00:15:49.140
I'm sure she's okay, right?

00:15:54.840 --> 00:15:58.140
Oh, what am I doing here?

00:15:58.850 --> 00:16:03.600
I should never have come to the capital 
if all it means is suffering like this...

00:16:04.060 --> 00:16:07.230
I had such high hopes when I left Taurus.

00:16:07.230 --> 00:16:09.570
What am I doing?

00:16:21.290 --> 00:16:23.210
What did you speak about?

00:16:24.340 --> 00:16:26.930
Maybe what you said was right.

00:16:27.670 --> 00:16:30.460
Humans are foolish, and they're thoughtless.

00:16:30.460 --> 00:16:32.470
And they're greedy, to boot.

00:16:33.430 --> 00:16:35.590
I'm like that, too, so I 
guess that makes me human.

00:16:36.570 --> 00:16:37.900
Left to its own devices,

00:16:37.900 --> 00:16:39.930
the species known as humanity 
would eventually go extinct.

00:16:40.600 --> 00:16:45.060
That is why we are here, to see to 
it that humanity continues to exist.

00:16:45.060 --> 00:16:48.940
If... If Pacifica turns 16,

00:16:48.940 --> 00:16:50.900
what do you think will happen?

00:16:51.900 --> 00:16:54.320
Will this world flicker out and disappear?

00:16:54.320 --> 00:16:56.570
Will it just be humanity that's wiped out?

00:16:56.570 --> 00:16:59.910
We don't know what that system 
is intended to do, either.

00:17:01.240 --> 00:17:04.370
We merely carry out the mission 
that was assigned to us.

00:17:05.370 --> 00:17:09.290
And then I got a job at that playhouse!

00:17:09.290 --> 00:17:10.960
Can you guess what I did there?

00:17:10.960 --> 00:17:13.340
I played a horse's legs! A horse's legs!

00:17:13.340 --> 00:17:15.840
I guess it's too much to 
expect to play a princess,

00:17:15.840 --> 00:17:18.140
but a horse's legs? That's too much!

00:17:18.140 --> 00:17:21.100
Oh... I wish I could have seen it.

00:17:21.100 --> 00:17:23.060
What, a horse's legs?

00:17:23.600 --> 00:17:26.690
No, you being in a play

00:17:26.690 --> 00:17:30.240
and living a happy life 
with all sorts of people.

00:17:30.940 --> 00:17:34.900
Oh, right. You said that you have 
a daughter, didn't you, ma'am?

00:17:34.900 --> 00:17:36.650
You haven't seen her in a long time?

00:17:36.650 --> 00:17:42.240
No... I gave up my daughter 
when she was a little baby.

00:17:42.240 --> 00:17:43.290
Oh...

00:17:44.160 --> 00:17:47.000
I didn't even give her a name...

00:17:47.000 --> 00:17:48.590
I thought that if I did,

00:17:48.590 --> 00:17:50.620
I'd never be able to give her up...

00:17:51.090 --> 00:17:56.260
But it was impossible for 
me to keep her with me...

00:17:57.340 --> 00:17:59.590
So, what became of her?

00:18:00.680 --> 00:18:05.600
I heard from secondhand sources that she 
grew to be a carefree, cheerful girl.

00:18:05.600 --> 00:18:08.140
Really? I'm glad to hear it.

00:18:08.140 --> 00:18:12.980
I've prayed ever since that the day would 
come that I would be able to meet her.

00:18:12.980 --> 00:18:14.940
Yeah, I'm sure you will!

00:18:15.940 --> 00:18:16.890
Yes...

00:18:18.400 --> 00:18:20.910
I have someone that I want to see again, too.

00:18:22.530 --> 00:18:27.030
Well, he's... He's really gruff,

00:18:27.030 --> 00:18:28.920
and when we go to the baths, 
he always makes me wait.

00:18:28.920 --> 00:18:30.880
And he's really bad at 
drawing portraits, too.

00:18:30.880 --> 00:18:35.310
Well, he does have one or two 
good things about him, though.

00:18:36.420 --> 00:18:40.890
Well, I suppose you're old 
enough to fall in love now...

00:18:41.590 --> 00:18:45.060
Who said that I love him?!

00:18:52.690 --> 00:18:56.050
Say, ma'am?

00:19:01.070 --> 00:19:02.240
Ma'am?

00:19:04.830 --> 00:19:06.450
Hey, ma'am?

00:19:07.180 --> 00:19:08.410
Are you really okay?

00:19:08.410 --> 00:19:09.630
Ma'am!

00:19:12.500 --> 00:19:14.790
Hey! Somebody, come here!

00:19:14.790 --> 00:19:16.750
Come quick! Somebody, come here!

00:19:17.340 --> 00:19:19.260
Get over here <i>now</i>!

00:19:20.260 --> 00:19:21.220
What do you want?! Quiet down!

00:19:21.800 --> 00:19:23.800
The lady in the cell next door isn't well!

00:19:23.800 --> 00:19:25.220
Please! Call a doctor!

00:19:25.220 --> 00:19:26.980
Keep it quiet!

00:19:35.060 --> 00:19:36.820
H-Hey, wait a minute!

00:19:36.820 --> 00:19:39.490
Please... Could you...

00:19:39.990 --> 00:19:43.450
Could... you tell me your name?

00:19:43.450 --> 00:19:46.300
My name? It's Pamela.

00:19:47.080 --> 00:19:48.450
Pamela...

00:19:49.060 --> 00:19:51.370
I'm sure you'll get out of here.

00:19:51.370 --> 00:19:54.460
That's right! Once you give 
up, you've already lost!

00:19:54.460 --> 00:19:55.920
So let's both hang in there, okay?

00:19:56.910 --> 00:19:58.580
Of course...

00:20:01.080 --> 00:20:02.250
Ma'am?

00:20:04.480 --> 00:20:06.050
Ma'am!

00:20:06.050 --> 00:20:09.280
Pamela... Could you do something for me?

00:20:10.230 --> 00:20:15.810
I'd like you... to call me 
"mother" before I die...

00:20:16.360 --> 00:20:17.860
Before you die?

00:20:18.770 --> 00:20:20.940
Hey, don't talk like that.

00:20:20.940 --> 00:20:22.280
Pretend that you're my daughter...

00:20:23.410 --> 00:20:24.780
Please...

00:20:26.570 --> 00:20:29.490
I can't... I can't call you that.

00:20:29.490 --> 00:20:31.750
Because once I do, you'll...

00:20:32.330 --> 00:20:34.960
Don't die! I'll come up with something!

00:20:36.380 --> 00:20:38.000
Don't... You can't...

00:20:38.000 --> 00:20:38.960
Don't give up!

00:20:39.400 --> 00:20:42.670
I'm sorry, Pamela...

00:20:43.800 --> 00:20:45.680
No... Don't die!

00:20:45.680 --> 00:20:46.640
Say something!

00:20:47.100 --> 00:20:48.140
Hey! Don't!

00:20:48.500 --> 00:20:50.560
Please, hang on!

00:20:50.560 --> 00:20:52.020
Mother?

00:20:52.730 --> 00:20:54.440
Mother?!

00:20:54.440 --> 00:20:55.520
Mother...

00:20:58.270 --> 00:20:59.900
Mother!

00:21:16.580 --> 00:21:21.730
<i>A blessing of rain falls quietly. (Falls.)</i>

00:21:21.730 --> 00:21:27.050
<i>Droplets of my love, 
which fall for someone...</i>

00:21:27.050 --> 00:21:34.230
<i>who is still waiting in a land far away.</i>

00:21:34.230 --> 00:21:40.020
<i>The morning wind blows, caressing 
my cheek. (What was that...)</i>

00:21:40.020 --> 00:21:45.150
<i>Did you feel something, feel something 
just now? (...on my cheek?)</i>

00:21:45.150 --> 00:21:48.320
<i>It goes up to the one and only sky... 
(More certain than anything.)</i>

00:21:48.320 --> 00:21:53.370
<i>a sky which has a fixed, certain meaning.</i>

00:21:53.370 --> 00:21:59.920
<i>I come to a stop in the shadow 
of clouds that chase after me.</i>

00:21:59.920 --> 00:22:03.380
<i>This journey of the heart 
that I wish to gaze upon...</i>

00:22:03.380 --> 00:22:06.590
<i>goes on forever and goes on forever.</i>

00:22:06.590 --> 00:22:13.220
<i>One day I will chance upon the 
voice I've not heard in so long.</i>

00:22:13.220 --> 00:22:15.180
<i>Alainn la-li-la.</i>

00:22:15.180 --> 00:22:19.900
<i>At last the ship sets sail, sets sail. 
(The ship glides on forever...)</i>

00:22:19.900 --> 00:22:25.190
<i>Yes, believe in this wide world... 
(...to the edge of seas unknown.)</i>

00:22:25.190 --> 00:22:28.530
<i>and go off into the distance.</i>

00:22:28.530 --> 00:22:32.630
<i>And onwards into the future.</i>

00:22:33.450 --> 00:22:46.460
"Next Time"

00:22:34.040 --> 00:22:36.620
Pacifica is taken out of her cell 
and brought before the king.

00:22:36.620 --> 00:22:39.000
It seems like the king is 
afraid of Pacifica, though.

00:22:39.000 --> 00:22:40.920
But General Peters-Stahl, who knows no fear,

00:22:40.920 --> 00:22:44.460
seems to be trying to make a deal with 
the Peacemaker Cz using Pacifica.

00:22:44.460 --> 00:22:47.090
It sure is audacious to try to bargain 
with beings who are like gods, isn't it?

00:22:47.090 --> 00:22:48.320
Next time on <i>Scrapped Princess</i>,

00:22:48.320 --> 00:22:49.680
"Prelude to the Divinely-Ordered Collapse."

00:22:49.680 --> 00:22:50.470
Please tune in!
